---
title: Penne alla vodka
servings: 4
yield: 4 to 6 servings
tags: [italian, vegetarian, weeknight]
cuisine: italian
time: 45 minutes
source: Penne alla Vodka by Jennifer Segal, Once Upon a Chef, https://www.onceuponachef.com/recipes/penne-alla-vodka.html
---

Put a #large pot{} of well-salted water on to boil.

Melt the @unsalted butter{3%tbsp} in a #3-quart saucepan{} over medium heat. Add
the @yellow onion{3/4%cup}(finely chopped) and cook ~{4%minutes} until soft and
translucent.

Add the @garlic{3%cloves}(minced) and @red pepper flakes{1/2%tsp} and stir
~{30%seconds}.

Add the @whole peeled tomatoes{28%oz}(chopped, with their juice),
@tomato paste{2%tbsp}, @salt{1%tsp}, @sugar{1/2%tsp} and @vodka{1/3%cup}. Bring
to a boil, then simmer briskly, uncovered, ~{10%minutes}.

Meanwhile cook the @dried pasta{16%oz}(penne) until just short of al dente. Save about a cup
of the pasta water, then drain.

Stir the @heavy cream{2/3%cup} into the sauce and simmer ~{3%minutes}. Blend
with an #immersion blender{} until mostly smooth, leaving a few small pieces.

Tip the sauce over the penne and bring to a gentle boil over medium-high heat,
stirring, for a few minutes until the sauce clings. Loosen with pasta water if
it gets too thick.

Stir in the @basil{3%tbsp}(chopped), season to taste, and serve with
@parmesan{}(Parmigiano-Reggiano, finely grated).
